Day 2 call opener

Hi [Name], [Caller] from Spendflo. Sid sent a note about supplier contract redlining in Coupa. We’re implementing a workflow that returns a policy-based redline and change summary for Legal’s review. Is this an area you own?

If they own the workflow

Would a sample agreement and the resulting redline be useful? You could assess the output before deciding whether a conversation makes sense.

If they invite a conversation

Does procurement prepare a first pass today, or does supplier paper go straight to Legal? Which agreement type creates the most repeated review work?

If they are the wrong person

