Launch review

The outbound owner confirms current contacts and account routing. Product confirms the demonstrable scope, contract permissions and approval behaviour. The sample is ready to share. Customer references are approved or anonymous. Messages describe an implementation underway and contain no unsubstantiated results, timelines or pricing.

Review after the campaign

Assess which roles replied, whether the sample earned interest, what buyers said was already solved, and where work actually sits. Use those observations to adjust the next cohort. One account’s outcome cannot establish a channel benchmark or repeatable conversion rate.



Sonoco GTM plan

Lead with one job to validate: preparing software renewals for an owner decision before the notice deadline. Position Flo around the work still performed manually, if any, within Sonoco’s established procurement automation environment. Do not assume that Coupa or Fairmarkit leaves this work uncovered.

The proposed job

Assemble the contract terms, cancellation deadline, accountable owner, supplier context and pricing benchmark; get the owner’s decision in time to act; then initiate a prefilled renewal request in Coupa where supported. This reflects the Datavant implementation scope, rather than proof that Sonoco needs the same workflow.

Why this account is worth investigating

Sonoco confirms Coupa for indirect purchase orders and supplier onboarding. Fairmarkit documents a Coupa-integrated request-to-sourcing workflow. Sonoco’s October 2026 results cite continued procurement savings and cost pressure. These establish fit and an existing investment in automation; they do not establish missed notices or renewal leakage.

Prioritize the possible gaps

Priority | Job to test | Disqualifying answer

First | Renewal preparation and owner decision before the notice deadline. | Contract data, timely decisions and renewal initiation are already covered.

Second | Commercial questions and policy exceptions across contracts. | An existing contract tool answers those questions adequately.

Third | Contract review and the manual contract-to-PR step. | No material manual workload or existing automation covers it.



Start with the process owner

Elizabeth Mozley is a credible first route. A current Fairmarkit page identifies her as Director, Source to Pay at Sonoco. Confirm her remit; ask for the IT or software category owner if renewal preparation sits elsewhere. Bring in the Coupa owner and Legal after the business gap is clear. Do not begin with the CFO.

Evidence boundaries

Fairmarkit markets expiration monitoring and sourcing triggered before contracts lapse. Ask about Sonoco’s deployed scope; do not claim Fairmarkit only covers new purchases. The divestitures are confirmed historical events, but unresolved TSAs, duplicate licences and renewal chaos are unverified. A supplier portal contract reference does not establish full Coupa CLM deployment or its absence.



Sonoco coordinated outbound cadence

Use the same account coordination discipline as Mattel: one owner, recipient-local business hours, and scheduled outreach paused on any reply. This is a suggested 15-business-day experiment, not a separate full sequence for every contact.

Day | Channel | Action

1 | Email | Siddharth sends Elizabeth the renewal preparation question.

2 | Call | Validate ownership and whether the preparation is already covered.

4 | LinkedIn | Send a contextual connection request.

6 | Email | Clarify the distinction between a date alert and a decision-ready renewal.

8 | Call | Ask which part, if any, still requires manual preparation.

10 | Referral | If unengaged, verify one IT/software category owner. Use the secondary email; do not invent a referral.

12 | LinkedIn | If connected and unengaged, ask one concise coverage question.

15 | Email | Close the loop. Stop the active sequence if unanswered.



